---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site keeps when you visit or send me a message, and how to get it deleted."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-10 sm:px-6">
    <header class="mb-6">
      <h1 class="text-2xl font-light tracking-tight sm:text-[30px]">Privacy</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="copy">
      <p>
        This site has no cookies and no ads. Here's what it does keep, and what
        I do with it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-light tracking-tight">Messages</h2>
      <p>
        When you send me a message, the form passes along your name, email
        address and message, plus the time you sent it. I only use them to
        reply, and to arrange a print if it comes to that. Nobody else gets
        them, and you won't end up on a mailing list.
      </p>
      <p>
        Messages are kept in my own Microsoft Azure account, on servers in the
        US. They stay there until I delete them. Ask through the form if you'd
        like yours gone and I'll take care of it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The form also counts how many messages come from one connection each
        hour, to keep spam down. It does that with a scrambled code made from
        your IP address, so the address itself is never saved.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-light tracking-tight">Visit counts</h2>
      <p>
        Each page you open is noted, along with how long you stayed on it. If
        another site sent you here, its name is saved too (google.com, say,
        never the full link).
      </p>
      <p>
        Visitors are counted without the site knowing who they are. It mixes
        your IP address and browser with the date and a secret key, then keeps
        only the scrambled result. That code changes every day, so visits on
        different days can't be linked. Your IP address is never stored.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-light tracking-tight">On your device</h2>
      <p>
        Your light or dark setting is saved in your browser, and so is your
        progress on the hobby pages, like the tide pool critters you've found.
        None of it leaves your device, and clearing this site's data in your
        browser wipes it.
      </p>
      <p>
        While a tab is open, it also holds a random code that matches each page
        view with how long it lasted. Closing the tab clears it.
      </p>
      <p>
        The selfie to bird generator reads your photo right on your device. It's
        never uploaded.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-light tracking-tight">Other sites</h2>
      <p>
        The site runs on Microsoft Azure, and their servers handle every
        request, like any web host.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some hobby pages load photos and sightings straight from iNaturalist.
        When they do, your browser connects to iNaturalist, which sees your IP
        address like any site you visit.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing here follows you around other sites, and no one else gets to
        either. Visit counts work the same whether or not your browser sends Do
        Not Track. I don't sell or pass on anything about you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-light tracking-tight">Your data</h2>
      <p>
        Send me a message if you want to know what I have from you, or want it
        fixed or deleted, and I'll sort it out. If any of this changes, I'll
        update this page and the date below.
      </p>
      <button
        type="button"
        class="linkbtn draw"
        data-contact-open
        data-contact-message="I have a question about my data."
      >
        <span>Ask about your data</span>
      </button>

      <p class="updated">
        Last updated <time datetime="2026-10-14">October 14, 2026</time>
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-12">
      <a class="u-label" href="/">← All sessions</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .copy {
    max-width: 65ch;
  }
  .copy p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .copy h2 {
    margin: 44px 0 12px;
  }
  .copy .updated {
    margin-top: 32px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    font-size: 13px;
  }
</style>
